    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d759">

                <pb facs="0928" n="920" sameAs="frus:frus1938v02/pg920"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867N.01/1079</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chief of the Division of Near Eastern Affairs</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Murray</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Minister Resident in Iraq</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Knabenshue</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-05-13">May 13, 1938</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Paul</hi>: Acknowledgment is made of your
                    letters of March 17 and March 31, 1938, concerning the Nuri–Magnus negotiations
                    which you had previously reported at such informative length.</p>
                <p>While we have heard nothing officially as yet of the continued activities of Nuri
                    he would appear clearly indicated as the inspirer of the proposal voiced by the
                    Emir of Trans-Jordan and reported in the <hi rendition="#italic">New York
                        Times</hi> of May 8, 1938. A copy of the report<anchor n="41"
                        xml:id="d759-f1"/> in question is enclosed as of possible interest to
                    you.</p>
                <p>It is expected, of course, that we shall be kept informed of the progress of any
                    negotiations Nuri Pasha may have in Syria or Palestine by one or the other of
                    our Consulates General there. Any information, however, which you may obtain on
                    the subject in Baghdad will be welcomed as always.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wallace Murray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
